# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*

# testing
/coverage
/e2e/screenshots/
/.screenshots/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/playwright/.cache/

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# claude code per-user config, EXCEPT the sub-agent definitions: those are
# project process, not personal preference, and they carry the project's hard-won
# constraints. Excluding the contents rather than the directory itself is
# required — git never descends into an excluded directory, so a `!` rule under
# `.claude/` would never be evaluated.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/

# local-only media / uploads (photos live in R2, never in the repo)
/uploads/
*.raw
*.cr2
*.nef
*.arw

# SDD skill-registry cache (regenerated locally)
.atl/*.cache.json

# Design working files (IG-sourced references, screenshots, raw crops) — not app code.
# EXCEPT the design-system mocks: they are the approved visual source of truth for
# epics #125 (dashboard) and #140 (client gallery), and every slice in those epics has
# an acceptance criterion that says "matches the mock". While /design/ was ignored
# wholesale, `git worktree add` never populated it, so no agent worktree could see the
# mock — #128 verified against it only because it happened to use an absolute path,
# while #127 concluded the file did not exist. Same criterion, opposite outcomes, both
# reported honestly. See task #170.
#
# The negation needs all four lines: git does not descend into an ignored directory,
# so re-including a file inside one requires un-ignoring each parent first.
#
# Deliberately still ignored: design/assets/ (4.6 MB of JPEGs and Instagram-sourced
# reference material — not ours to redistribute, and binaries in git history are
# forever). dashboard.html and client.html are fully self-contained, no images, no
# external URLs. home.html does reference design/system/assets/, which stays ignored;
# its <img> tags will not resolve on a fresh clone. That is accepted: the mock is read
# for its markup and CSS, not its photographs.
/design/*
!/design/system/
/design/system/*
!/design/system/*.html
kanban/
